{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for Keepcase, the design system vhs-blog-theme defines for itself (design-system/keepcase.tokens.json, a local source). Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. Keepcase is dark by design, so every named DDD color points at one fixed room or case color: white is the room's warm ink and coalyGray is the post panel, which is the pair DDD blocks use on a dark page. Kept as DDD on purpose: light, regular and medium weights (Archivo has them at DDD's values), state opacities, control heights and border widths (Keepcase has no rules of its own there), and heading/body sizes (posts keep DDD's reading sizes). The per-case palettes are not mapped: they belong to each tape, not to the page.",
  "system": "keepcase",
  "title": "Keepcase",
  "prefix": "Keepcase",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/haxtheweb/webcomponents/tree/master/elements/vhs-blog-theme",
  "sources": [
    {
      "local": true,
      "file": "design-system/keepcase.tokens.json",
      "format": "dtcg",
      "prefix": "--keepcase-",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "copyright": "Copyright 2026 The Pennsylvania State University"
    }
  ],
  "fonts": [
